# Snake Atlas — Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** November 9, 2026
**Developer:** AxiomaraGames
**Contact:** axiomaragames@gmail.com

Snake Atlas ("the app") is a snake encyclopedia: species profiles, identification from a photo, care, health, behavior and breeding guides, venom and snakebite safety information, habitats and a quiz. This policy explains what information the app handles, the licences of the software it is built with, and who made the images in it.

## Summary

The app does not collect, transmit, sell or share any personal data. Everything you add to it stays on your device.

## Information the app stores on your device

To work, the app saves the following, **only on your device**:

- **Favorites:** the species you save
- **Discovered species:** the species profiles you have opened
- **Quiz:** your best quiz score
- **Free version allowances:** how many identifications and quiz rounds you have used today

This information is never sent to us or to anyone else. You can erase it in Settings > Reset my data. It is also deleted when you uninstall the app or clear its data in your device's settings.

**Photos and snake identification:** when you identify a snake, you take a photo with your device's camera app or choose one from your device. An image-recognition (AI) model built into the app looks at the photo on your device, without an internet connection. The photo is never uploaded or stored by the app. The app does not ask for camera permission itself: taking a photo opens your device's own camera app, which hands that one photo back.

## Purchases

The app is free to download. The full version is a one-time in-app purchase made through Google Play. Google Play handles the payment under Google's own terms and privacy policy; we never see your payment details. The app only asks Google Play whether the full version has been bought on your Google account, so it can unlock it, also after a reinstall or on a new device.

## What the app does not do

- It does not ask you to create an account or sign in.
- It does not connect to our servers or any other server, apart from Google Play for the purchase described above. All species profiles, guides and images are built into the app. The link to this policy opens in your web browser.
- It does not collect analytics, crash reports, location, contacts or device identifiers.
- It does not show ads and contains no advertising or tracking software.
- It does not use your microphone.

## Safety information

The venom, first aid, health and care information in the app is general guidance for education. It is not medical or veterinary advice and does not replace a doctor, a poison center or a veterinarian. Photo identification is made by an AI model and can be wrong, even when it shows a high percentage: never use the app to decide whether a snake is safe to approach or handle. After a snakebite, call your local emergency number at once.

## Children

The app is a general reference about snakes and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone, including children, because we collect no information at all.

## Changes to this policy

If this policy changes, the new version will be published at this address with a new effective date. Because the app collects no data, any change will not affect information you have already given us.

## Contact

Questions about this policy: axiomaragames@gmail.com

