# Image Credits

Snake Atlas uses photographs shared by observers on [iNaturalist](https://www.inaturalist.org) and contributors to [Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org), under the licences named for each one: CC0 (public domain dedication), CC BY or CC BY-SA. Every photograph was cropped, resized and color-adjusted for the app; no other changes were made. Photographs under a CC BY-SA licence are, as adapted, shared under that same licence. The photographers do not endorse Snake Atlas.

The following artwork was created for Snake Atlas with an AI image generator (ChatGPT, OpenAI) and is not a photograph of a real animal or place: the title screen picture, the snake logo, the app icon, the page background, the pictures at the top of the Care Guide, Venom & Safety, Health, Behavior and Breeding guides, the sample photo on the Identify screen, the eight habitat pictures, and any species image marked "AI illustration" below. The AxiomaraGames logo belongs to AxiomaraGames.

## The identification model

The snake identifier is an image-recognition model (EfficientNet-B2, starting from torchvision's ImageNet weights, BSD licence) trained by AxiomaraGames on about 30,000 photographs from [iNaturalist](https://www.inaturalist.org) research-grade observations and [Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org), all under licences that allow commercial use (CC0, public domain, CC BY or CC BY-SA). The training photographs are not included in the app; only the model learnt from them is. The model runs on your device with [ONNX Runtime](https://onnxruntime.ai) (MIT licence, Microsoft).

